rule: ELIM-G-3
One copy of applyTwice per static function argument; the static argument's
closure is the key, compared by label.
CHECK-DAG: -- specialization of Main.applyTwice(lam{{[0-9]+}}[]; _:Int)
CHECK-DAG: -- specialization of Main.applyTwice(lam{{[0-9]+}}[]; _:Int)
CHECK-DAG: Main.applyTwice#1 (%{{[0-9]+}} : w Int) : Int =
CHECK-DAG: Main.applyTwice#2 (%{{[0-9]+}} : w Int) : Int =
CHECK-DAG: add_Int(1:Int, %{{[0-9]+}})
CHECK-DAG: mul_Int(2:Int, %{{[0-9]+}})
rule: CORE-OPT-1
First-order calls with runtime arguments stay calls; MLIR inlines them.
CHECK-DAG: = Main.applyTwice#1(%{{[0-9]+}})
CHECK-DAG: = Main.applyTwice#2(%{{[0-9]+}})
